invariant: INV-26
file: src/aes.c
catches: aes_suite_test
reason: aes_traffic_key_load records no pointer to the owner's stored powers,
  so every seal and open computes the powers of its key again, as before
  decision 234. Every byte is the same, and only the instructions a record
  costs are wrong. The design refuses a silent fall back.
  bin/aes_suite_test changes one bit of a direction's first stored power
  and requires another tag for the same record, under each ch_cfg.cpu
  value that names a kernel, which holds only where the seal reads the
  stored bytes (test/ghash_powers_tests.h).

--- old
    k->ghash_powers = powers;
--- new
    (void)powers;
    k->ghash_powers = NULL;
